    "detailed_description": "<strong><i>Drawn to a mysterious cathedral, a boy sets out to unlock its secret.</i></strong><br><br>Traverse calm and colorful landscapes, where reflexes, persistence, and a sense of adventure drive you forward in this exploration-based platformer.<br><br>Run, jump, climb, and swim your way through <strong>(10) atmospheric settings</strong>, with each offering a distinct look and unique features.<br><br>Gather crystals, collect keys, unlock doors, and navigate environmental dangers while steering clear of <strong>over (20) perilous creatures</strong>.<br><br>Performed and recorded using live audio, <strong>(12) original songs</strong> create an ambient soundtrack to capture the mood and feel of each setting.<br><br>Unlocking each of the <strong>(14) chapters</strong> will allow you to continue your journey between sessions or replay select scenes.    <br><br>Full controller support.<br><br>Keyboard controls:<br><i>Movement - arrows and/or WASD keys<br>Jump/Select - CTRL and/or spacebar<br>Menu - ESC</i><br><br>Between two and three hours of gameplay for experienced players while first-timers can expect this timeframe to double or triple!<br><br>With its rich visuals, thoughtful soundtrack, and simple mechanics, <strong>The Boy and the Cathedral</strong> is a modern take on classic gaming.",
    "about_the_game": "<strong><i>Drawn to a mysterious cathedral, a boy sets out to unlock its secret.</i></strong><br><br>Traverse calm and colorful landscapes, where reflexes, persistence, and a sense of adventure drive you forward in this exploration-based platformer.<br><br>Run, jump, climb, and swim your way through <strong>(10) atmospheric settings</strong>, with each offering a distinct look and unique features.<br><br>Gather crystals, collect keys, unlock doors, and navigate environmental dangers while steering clear of <strong>over (20) perilous creatures</strong>.<br><br>Performed and recorded using live audio, <strong>(12) original songs</strong> create an ambient soundtrack to capture the mood and feel of each setting.<br><br>Unlocking each of the <strong>(14) chapters</strong> will allow you to continue your journey between sessions or replay select scenes.    <br><br>Full controller support.<br><br>Keyboard controls:<br><i>Movement - arrows and/or WASD keys<br>Jump/Select - CTRL and/or spacebar<br>Menu - ESC</i><br><br>Between two and three hours of gameplay for experienced players while first-timers can expect this timeframe to double or triple!<br><br>With its rich visuals, thoughtful soundtrack, and simple mechanics, <strong>The Boy and the Cathedral</strong> is a modern take on classic gaming.",
